Welded, brazed and bonded connections (@mech-permanent-joints: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @mechanical-engineering, #source "../sources/FUNdaMENTALS-of-Design-Slocum.lingua#r_58Q6VQJ3FXXGXRBJ3DK0AVC3WQ", #source "../sources/Applied-Mechanics-of-Solids-Bower.lingua#r_109WFZBWMEMGHV9TGFD22H2F1W", #mechanical-engineering "Seals-leakage-friction-and-the-condition-of-surfaces.lingua#r_5TC8MG4GQKQ1YEVSNG6G1EV2Y5") { r_7GS9WVN78MJX9FTD3H0RQXEPCY
**Read:** [FUNdaMENTALS of Design — Alexander Slocum](../sources/FUNdaMENTALS-of-Design-Slocum.lingua#r_58Q6VQJ3FXXGXRBJ3DK0AVC3WQ), topic 9; [Applied Mechanics of Solids — Allan F. Bower](../sources/Applied-Mechanics-of-Solids-Bower.lingua#r_109WFZBWMEMGHV9TGFD22H2F1W), material behavior, stress concentrations and failure. Follow the shared metallurgy route for processing and weld-condition evidence.

A permanent joint changes both the load path and the material or interface that carries it. Welds introduce geometry, heat-affected material, residual stress and possible imperfections. Brazing transfers load through a filler/interface system without the same base-material melting. Adhesive joints depend on surface preparation, chemistry, thickness, cure and environment.

A single-lap bonded joint carries an eccentric load path that creates peel and bending as well as shear. Dividing force by overlap area cannot establish its peak stress or durability. Increasing overlap length can have diminishing benefit when load transfer remains concentrated near the ends. Similarly, a weld's nominal throat calculation does not replace assessment of its local fatigue detail.

**Work:** Compare bolted, welded, brazed and bonded solutions to the same connection. Trace force and deformation through each, including thermal mismatch and a plausible imperfection. Specify what process information and inspection evidence would establish the delivered condition. Compare repairability and disassembly without assuming that an invisible interface is a perfect bond.

